# core/data/talk/grammar/en/topic_people.tlk - T5b-TOPIC: replies by topic kind (root=people) for
# ASK_ABOUT, ASK_OPINION, TELL and the opinion acts. The people root holds relations and social
# words, but also bodies, clothes, looks and personalities, so the lines here talk about the word
# itself and never assume a person; the person-only ones carry needs: x.person (lore.cast too).
# Kid-safe. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.
@rule core.ask_about.people_pro guard: root=people&stance=pro act: opine_pos
  "{x:cap}? Love it. Best thing on this street, and the street is mostly fog."
  "{x:cap}! That's a happy word. I'd put it on a mug."
  "{x:cap}? Oh, the good stuff. I save it for Sundays."
  "Anyone who says {x} gets my full attention. And my last biscuit."
  "{x:cap}? Warms me right up, every time. I respect that."
  "I wrote {x} on my list of good things. The list is short."
@rule core.ask_about.people_con guard: root=people&stance=con act: opine_neg
  "{x:cap}? We don't speak, me and that. We nod."
  "{x:cap}? It borrowed my good mood in spring. It's autumn."
  "I'm being polite about {x}. That's why I'm quiet."
  "{x:cap}? Somebody laughed at my hat over that. It's a good hat."
  "I keep a distance from {x}. About two porches."
  "{x:cap}. Next question. A kinder one, please."
@rule core.ask_about.people_neu guard: root=people&stance=neutral act: answer
  "{x:cap}? I've seen a few. Nice enough, mostly taller than me."
  "I couldn't pick {x} out of a lineup. Pick me out of one, I'm easy."
  "{x:cap}? Ask the mayor. He knows about everything and says so."
  "A friend of a friend knows about {x}. That's as close as I've been."
  "{x:cap}? I'd need a name tag first. And lighting."
  "Things like {x} come and go. I stay and nap."
@rule core.ask_about.people_joke guard: root=people act: joke
  "{x:cap}? Hold on, I had a joke for that. It wandered off."
  "{x:cap}? I'd tell you, but it'd be all over town by lunch."
  "{x:cap} and I have a bit. It's mostly staring."
@rule core.ask_about.people_more guard: root=people act: answer
  "{x:cap}? Everybody's got one. Mine is unremarkable." needs: x.countable
  "{x:cap}? Good company, in small doses."
  "We have a few of those in town. One waves too much." needs: x.countable
  "{x:cap}? I'd lend mine out. Nobody asks."
@rule core.ask_opinion.people guard: root=people act: answer
  "My opinion of {x}? Warm. Slightly damp, but warm."
  "{x:cap}? Solid. I'd keep it around."
  "I think {x} means well. So does the fog, and look at the fog."
  "{x:cap}? Trustworthy. On a good day, on most days."
  "Honest take on {x}: good company, loud at breakfast."
  "{x:cap}? Four out of five handshakes."
@rule core.tell.people_pro guard: root=people&stance=pro act: opine_pos
  "Ah, {x}! Lovely. Don't tell them I said so."
  "{x:cap}, yes! You know the good ones."
  "I like that you bring up {x}. It's a good sign in a person."
  "{x:cap}? I'd help it move house. That's how I rate things."
@rule core.tell.people_con guard: root=people&stance=con act: opine_neg
  "{x:cap}? Hm. I'm staying out of that, I have a hat to protect."
  "I'd keep my distance from {x}. And my ladder."
  "That's a lot to say about {x}. All of it is fair."
  "{x:cap}, huh. We'll talk later. Quietly."
@rule core.opine_pos.people_agree guard: root=people&stance=pro act: agree
  "Right? {x:cap} is a gem. A noisy gem."
  "Exactly. {x:cap} gets it. Gets all of it."
  "Yes. Give {x} a medal. A small one."
@rule core.opine_pos.people_disagree guard: root=people&stance=con act: disagree
  "Hm, I'd say {x} is fine. Fine and loud."
  "Not {x}! It fixed my gate once. Eventually."
@rule core.opine_neg.people_agree guard: root=people&stance=con act: agree
  "Ha, {x}. You noticed too. I thought it was only me."
  "Right? I said nothing. Loudly."
@rule core.opine_neg.people_disagree guard: root=people&stance=pro act: disagree
  "Go easy on {x}. It's had a week."
  "Oh, not {x}. It once carried my groceries. Some of them."
